Add dtiSplit, a CLI over TensorData's external-data split

TensorData.makeExternalData and makeCompactStore are reachable only from the
app's Optimize for Faster Loading action, which is gated to the Metal
performance tiers, while every server load path already opens with
externalStore and an .externalData read codec. This adds Apps:dtiSplit so a
repository copy can be pre-split ahead of first use, and --unsplit for the
inverse. New files, plus an Apps/BUILD target and a Package.swift product and
target pair. The tool verifies each file after writing it, because the
upstream helpers swallow their own errors.
